.TH DARPA_SPILLSERVER 3 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
darpa_spillserver \- Python library for NOvA accelerator event timestamps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
.B from darpa_spillserver.config import load_config
.B from darpa_spillserver.app import create_app
.B from darpa_spillserver.storage import SpillStore
.B from darpa_spillserver.signals import parse_signal, decode_event_word
.B from darpa_spillserver.novatime import parse_range, convert
.B from darpa_spillserver.client import SpillClient, Selection
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B darpa_spillserver
package implements the DARPA Spill Information Server. Its modules are layered
so that each is useful on its own, without running a server.
.SH MODULES
.SS darpa_spillserver.signals
The accelerator signal registry and the hardware's decode rules, ported from
.I NssSpillInfo::getSpillTypeFromEvent
in the
.B NovaSpillServer
package.
.TP
.BI decode_event_word( evt )
Decode a raw 16-bit event word to a
.BR SpillType .
.TP
.BI parse_signal( text )
Resolve
.BR $74 ", " 74 ", " 0x74
or a registry name to a
.B Signal
record.
.TP
.BI signals_for_type( spill_type )
Every signal decoding to that type. More than one means a stored record
carrying only the type is ambiguous.
.SS darpa_spillserver.novatime
Parsing human time expressions and converting between timescales. The
arithmetic is delegated to
.BR nova_time_decoder (3);
nothing here reimplements a conversion.
.TP
.BI parse_instant( text ", " now ", " tz ", " end_of_day )
Parse one time expression to NOvA ticks.
.TP
.BI parse_range( start ", " end ", " now ", " tz )
Resolve a pair into a half-open
.RI ( start ", " end )
tick range.
.TP
.BI convert( nova )
Render one tick count as a
.B ConvertedTime
carrying NOvA, UNIX, UTC and GPS forms.
.SS darpa_spillserver.storage
The SQLite archive.
.B SpillStore
is synchronous and thread-safe through per-thread connections; async callers
should wrap calls in
.IR asyncio.to_thread .
Inserts are idempotent on
.RI ( nova_time ", " spill_type ", " signal_code ", " source ).
Opening an archive from before sources existed migrates it in place, tagging
its events with the
.I legacy_source
name passed to the constructor.
.SS darpa_spillserver.tdu_client
An async HTTP client for the TDU's embedded web server, speaking both the
legacy single-event routes and the bulk
.I /spill_history
route, and tolerating the malformed JSON that
.B DumpSpillHistory
emits.
.SS darpa_spillserver.poller
The background ingest loops.
.B Poller
polls one source;
.B IngestManager
runs one per enabled source and applies runtime changes to them.
.SS darpa_spillserver.formats
CSV and JSON rendering, as streaming generators.
.SS darpa_spillserver.config
Configuration merged from five layers, each overriding the one before:
defaults, a YAML file, a
.B .env
file, the environment, and the command line.
.TP
.BI load_config( args ", " argv ", " environ ", " search_paths ", " dotenv_path )
Build a
.B Config
from all five layers.
.I dotenv_path
(default
.BR DOTENV_PATH ,
.IR ./.env )
is read when neither
.B \-\-env\-file
nor
.B $DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE
names a file;
.B None
reads none. Raises
.B ConfigError
on any malformed or inconsistent setting.
.TP
.BI read_dotenv( path )
Parse a
.B .env
file into a
.BR dict :
.IB KEY = VALUE
lines, blank lines and
.B #
comments skipped, a leading
.B export
ignored, one layer of matching quotes removed, no interpolation. Raises
.B ConfigError
if the file cannot be read or a line has no
.BR = .
.TP
.BI resolve_dotenv( explicit ", " environ ", " default )
Read the
.B .env
file named by
.IR explicit ,
else by
.B DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE
in
.IR environ ,
else
.I default
if it exists. An explicitly named file must exist.
.SS darpa_spillserver.client
A client for a running server's HTTP API, using only the standard library for
HTTP (PyYAML only to read a configuration file). It follows the contract in
.IR docs/CLIENT.md ,
shared with the C++ library
.BR darpa_spill_client (3).
.TP
\fBSpillClient(\fIurl\fB, \fItimeout\fB=30.0, \fIadmin_token\fB=\(dq\(dq, \fIca_file\fB=\(dq\(dq, \fIverify_tls\fB=True, \fItimezone\fB=\(dq\(dq)\fR
One server.
.I admin_token
is sent as
.B X\-Admin\-Token
when not empty;
.I timezone
is sent as
.B tz=
on time-bearing queries when not empty.
.B SpillClient.from_config(\fIconfig\fB)
builds one from a
.BR ClientConfig .
.TP
.BR health() ", " status() ", " sources() ", " signals() ", " types() ", " time_help()
The reference routes, each returning the parsed JSON.
.TP
.BI time_convert( t ", " tz )
One instant rendered as NOvA ticks, UNIX, UTC and GPS.
.TP
.BI latest( signal ", " sources )
The newest event, as
.BR {"event":\ {...}} .
.TP
.BI events( selection ", " limit ", " offset ", " descending ", " tz )
One page, as
.BR {"meta":\ ...,\ "events":\ [...]} ;
.B meta.total
is the number matching overall.
.TP
.BI events_csv( selection ", " limit ", " offset ", " descending ", " tz ", " columns )
One page as CSV text, with its
.B #
comment header.
.TP
.BI export( selection ", " out ", " fmt "=\(dqcsv\(dq, " tz ", " columns )
Stream every matching event to the binary file
.IR out ,
in 64 KiB chunks; returns the number of bytes written.
.TP
.BR admin_check() ", " update_source( \fIname\fR ", " \fIenabled\fR ", " \fIbase_url\fR ) ", " reset_source( \fIname\fR )
Source administration; need the admin token.
.TP
.BI request( method ", " path ", " params ", " body )
.TQ
.BI stream( method ", " path ", " params )
The transport under every call:
.B request
returns a
.B Response
.RB ( status ", " headers ", " body ", " json() ", " text );
.B stream
yields the body in chunks.
.TP
.BI Selection( start ", " end ", " signals ", " types ", " sources )
Which events to ask for; every field optional. Times are any expression the
server accepts.
.TP
.BI encode_query( params )
Percent-encode an ordered list of
.RI ( name ", " value )
pairs per RFC 3986, so
.B $74
becomes
.BR %2474 .
.TP
.B ClientConfig
The settings
.BR url ", " timeout ", " admin_token ", " admin_token_file ", "
.BR ca_file ", " verify_tls ", " format ", " timezone ,
with
.B resolved_token()
(the token, read from
.B admin_token_file
if set) and
.B to_yaml()
(the
.B \-\-print\-config
layout, token hidden).
.TP
.BI load_client_config( config_file ", " env_file ", " overrides ", " environ ", " search_paths ", " dotenv_path )
Merge defaults, the YAML file's
.B client:
section, the
.B .env
file, the
.B DARPA_SPILL_CLIENT_
environment variables and
.I overrides
(command line;
.B None
values ignored), in rising precedence. Raises
.B ConfigError
on an unreadable file, unknown key or bad value.
.TP
.B SpillClientError
Base of every error the client raises.
.B SpillHTTPError
is an HTTP error status, with
.BR status ", " message " and " hint
read from the server's error body.
.B SpillConnectionError
means the server could not be reached (DNS, refused, TLS or timeout).
.SS darpa_spillserver.client_cli
.BR darpa-spill-client (1).
.BI main( argv ", " out ", " err )
runs it and returns the exit status;
.I out
is a binary stream so that output is written byte for byte.
.BR cell() ", " flatten() ", " render_table() " and " render_csv()
implement the output rules shared with
.BR darpa-spill-client-cpp (1).
.SS darpa_spillserver.pages
Content for the
.IR /about ,
.I /api
and
.I /sitemap
pages.
.BI api_context( schema )
and
.BI sitemap_groups( schema ", " auth_enabled )
are generated from the application's OpenAPI schema, so a new route appears
without anyone remembering to add it;
.BI sitemap_xml( base_url ", " schema )
renders a sitemaps.org
.BR urlset ;
.BI about_context( config ", " state )
reads installed dependency versions from package metadata.
.SS darpa_spillserver.api ", " darpa_spillserver.app
The FastAPI routes and the application factory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read an archive directly:
.PP
.RS
.EX
from darpa_spillserver.storage import SpillStore
from darpa_spillserver.novatime import parse_range, convert
from darpa_spillserver.signals import parse_signal

store = SpillStore("spills.db")
start, end = parse_range("2026-07-01", "today")
signal = parse_signal("$74")

page = store.query(start_nova=start, end_nova=end,
                   spill_types=[signal.spill_type])
for event in page.events:
    print(convert(event.nova_time).utc)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build an application for testing, without contacting a TDU:
.PP
.RS
.EX
from darpa_spillserver.app import create_app
from darpa_spillserver.config import Config

config = Config()
config.storage.path = ":memory:"
app = create_app(config, start_ingest=False)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Query a running server:
.PP
.RS
.EX
from darpa_spillserver.client import SpillClient, Selection, SpillHTTPError

client = SpillClient("http://novadaq\-near\-gateway\-01.fnal.gov:8080")
try:
    page = client.events(Selection(start="today", signals=["$74"]), limit=100)
except SpillHTTPError as exc:
    print(exc.status, exc.message, exc.hint)
else:
    print(page["meta"]["total"], len(page["events"]))
with open("numi.csv", "wb") as out:
    client.export(Selection(start="\-1d", signals=["$74"]), out)
.EE
.RE
